  "emptyCanvasSuiteFooter": "A member of the EDACrux suite of products — edacrux.app",
  "@emptyCanvasSuiteFooter": {
    "description": "Suite-membership line at the foot of the empty-canvas (welcome) screen. The whole line is a link to the EDACrux suite site. \"edacrux.app\" must appear verbatim — the widget splits the sentence around it to underline the domain — but a translation that drops it still renders and is still followable, just without an underlined segment. \"EDACrux\" is one word and is never translated."
  },
  "emptyCanvasPeersHeading": "MORE FROM EDACRUX",
  "@emptyCanvasPeersHeading": {
    "description": "Section header above the three sibling-product rows at the foot of the empty-canvas (welcome) screen. Rendered upper-case in English as a small letter-spaced label, matching the \"RECENT FILES\" headers above it; a locale whose script has no case simply reads as a label. \"EDACrux\" is one word and is never translated."
  },
  "emptyCanvasPeerNetCrux": "See the logic behind the signal. Cross-probe a waveform straight into the schematic, and back.",
  "@emptyCanvasPeerNetCrux": {
    "description": "One line in the \"More from EDACrux\" section of the empty-canvas (welcome) screen, describing NetCrux to someone using WaveCrux. Written from THIS product's point of view on purpose — what NetCrux does for a WaveCrux user is not what it does for a user of another product — so do not reuse another repository's wording. Keep it to roughly one short sentence plus one more; the row wraps but is not a paragraph. Product names are never translated."
  },
  "emptyCanvasPeerLintCrux": "Catch it before you simulate it. Lint and CDC-check the RTL that produced this trace.",
  "@emptyCanvasPeerLintCrux": {
    "description": "One line in the \"More from EDACrux\" section of the empty-canvas (welcome) screen, describing LintCrux to someone using WaveCrux. Written from THIS product's point of view on purpose — what LintCrux does for a WaveCrux user is not what it does for a user of another product — so do not reuse another repository's wording. Keep it to roughly one short sentence plus one more; the row wraps but is not a paragraph. Product names are never translated."
  },
  "emptyCanvasPeerSimCrux": "Run the testbench that wrote this trace. Launch regressions and open the failures here.",
  "@emptyCanvasPeerSimCrux": {
    "description": "One line in the \"More from EDACrux\" section of the empty-canvas (welcome) screen, describing SimCrux to someone using WaveCrux. Written from THIS product's point of view on purpose — what SimCrux does for a WaveCrux user is not what it does for a user of another product — so do not reuse another repository's wording. Keep it to roughly one short sentence plus one more; the row wraps but is not a paragraph. Product names are never translated."
  },
